From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glenn Skrzypczak <glenn.skrzypczak@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:28:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: script: handle Esc press as close request (#49640)

This intercepts `esc` presses and runs the close request steps in order
to close the fullscreen and elements controlled by close watchers (only
dialogs for now, later popovers aswell).

Testing: Passes new web platform tests.
Fixes: #47236

Signed-off-by: Glenn Skrzypczak <glenn.skrzypczak@gmail.com>

Fork note: upstream 3e7d8ed44d7, which came after Servo 0.8.0, backported with expectation adjustments. On 0.8.0 the light-dismiss subtests of dialog-closedby, the cross-origin close-watcher iframe cases and the SpiderMonkey testdriver issue in dialog-cancel-events and dialog-cancel-preventDefault still fail, so their expectations are kept or added. Drop this patch at the first sync onto a release that contains #49640, where the source applies unchanged and the expectations are upstream's.

Validation: release builds on the host with SpiderMonkey (666 WPT files from the affected directories, all as expected) and with QuickJS on a local servo-quickjs branch carrying the unmerged WebAssembly and await-realm fixes (the focused 229-test set, all as expected; the full set's remaining unexpected results are origin-keyed expectations that the WebAssembly shim changes).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; backported from upstream #49640, expectations updated from the two-engine runs)
Signed-off-by: daodaoliehuo <352812717@qq.com>
